WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.209
I'm going to talk a little
about how Penajóia is organised,

2
00:00:04.293 --> 00:00:07.411
because we're not just anonymous people.

3
00:00:07.495 --> 00:00:13.736
We have an association: the Penajóia
Neighbourhood Community Association,

4
00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:18.033
which deals directly
with the IHRU and the City Council.

5
00:00:18.303 --> 00:00:20.314
We're organised by plot.

6
00:00:20.398 --> 00:00:23.823
I mean, work that the City Council itself,
the IHRU, should have done,

7
00:00:23.907 --> 00:00:27.370
we've already done,
which is organising the streets...

8
00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:34.090
The neighbourhood is divided into plots,
we have seven plots.

9
00:00:34.515 --> 00:00:36.813
I'm not going to say
here which plot I'm in,

10
00:00:36.897 --> 00:00:41.096
also because of your malice,
the nastiness that comes,

11
00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:45.673
because people only ever want
to point to what's bad.

12
00:00:46.044 --> 00:00:50.784
They never want to tell
that there are hard-fighting people here,

13
00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:54.480
hard-working people,
people who are here to grow.

14
00:00:54.564 --> 00:00:57.368
Because they're two
completely different things:

15
00:00:57.452 --> 00:01:04.267
coming to Portugal and living
in a room, living in a room, right?

16
00:01:04.418 --> 00:01:07.109
Where there's no life,
families have no life.

17
00:01:07.193 --> 00:01:09.497
Since we couldn't find that possibility,

18
00:01:09.581 --> 00:01:14.841
we built our houses ourselves
and organised the neighbourhood by plots.

19
00:01:14.925 --> 00:01:16.316
We have an association.

20
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.425
We're not anonymous people,
we're not unknown or uninformed.

21
00:01:20.509 --> 00:01:25.823
So, the neighbourhood...
Now we're going to do the new mapping,

22
00:01:26.374 --> 00:01:30.506
so we can number the houses
that aren't numbered,

23
00:01:30.837 --> 00:01:38.412
do a survey again,
to be sure how many of us there are.

24
00:01:38.963 --> 00:01:45.497
No, it's not that here, simply,

25
00:01:45.788 --> 00:01:48.920
everyone arrived
and built their house. No.

26
00:01:49.411 --> 00:01:54.244
Also to say that we've been
working with the parish council,

27
00:01:54.335 --> 00:01:58.154
we've been working with the City Council,
we're organised from the school,

28
00:01:58.238 --> 00:02:02.972
the children's nurseries, we've been doing
social work here in the neighbourhood.

29
00:02:03.403 --> 00:02:10.038
It's not simply because...
"No, we just built and moved in."

30
00:02:10.122 --> 00:02:12.769
It's not quite how people say, it's not.

31
00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:17.202
We're organised,
we've been fighting to get organised,

32
00:02:17.732 --> 00:02:24.390
we're trying to improve,
every moment, every day, every hour.

33
00:02:25.675 --> 00:02:29.750
So, this is still our neighbourhood,

34
00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:37.990
Penajóia. It's me speaking to you,
once again, Esvarena de Sousa.

35
00:02:38.335 --> 00:02:44.708
And I also wanted to, like, tell you,
or ask you: for those who are curious,

36
00:02:45.159 --> 00:02:48.897
we're open to spending time together,

37
00:02:48.981 --> 00:02:55.254
we're open to people who want to clear
up their doubts. You don't even know.

38
00:02:55.784 --> 00:03:03.784
You only judge from a distance,
from what you've heard, seen, right?

39
00:03:04.409 --> 00:03:11.342
But from a distance... You need
to come closer, get to know us up close,

40
00:03:11.632 --> 00:03:14.183
know who the people here are,

41
00:03:14.513 --> 00:03:20.320
know who lives here, who resides here,
and the work that's done here.

42
00:03:21.415 --> 00:03:23.546
We're not outcasts, once again.

43
00:03:23.681 --> 00:03:27.373
We're not idle people who don't work,
who don't do anything.

44
00:03:27.457 --> 00:03:34.780
It's a lie when they say we don't want
to pay for water or electricity.

45
00:03:35.516 --> 00:03:38.516
They always turn down this request.
We make the request,

46
00:03:39.663 --> 00:03:43.957
but it's a struggle with the IHRU...
Nobody wants to take responsibility.

47
00:03:44.967 --> 00:03:48.758
And then there's the issue
of illegal hook-ups.

48
00:03:48.842 --> 00:03:52.195
I myself, personally, spoke to the Mayor,

49
00:03:52.408 --> 00:03:58.606
to put an end once and for all
to these fights they talk about,

50
00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:01.200
illegal water and power hook-ups.

51
00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:05.062
We asked them to put in legal water here,
legal electricity here,

52
00:04:05.413 --> 00:04:11.366
so that there won't be any
kind of illegal hook-ups.

53
00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:15.450
And it's not our fault that we're not
paying for water or electricity, people.

54
00:04:15.559 --> 00:04:19.735
It's not our fault. So,

55
00:04:20.966 --> 00:04:25.890
that's more or less what I came
to talk about, what I'm bringing here,

56
00:04:28.347 --> 00:04:31.258
for those of you who are always curious,

57
00:04:31.388 --> 00:04:38.980
and also for those who come
to make malicious videos, right? Right?

58
00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:45.470
We are a really big community

59
00:04:47.702 --> 00:04:54.040
because of the housing crisis.
I repeat: because of the housing crisis.
